# Project: EZR eTurns MVP

A Next.js 16 App Router application for scheduling pickups, managing orders, and handling memberships with Stripe payments.

# Tech Stack

| Layer       | Technology                                  |
| ----------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Framework   | Next.js 16 (App Router)                     |
| React       | React 19                                    |
| Database    | Supabase (Postgres + Auth + RLS)            |
| Payments    | Stripe (Checkout, Webhooks, Subscriptions)  |
| Styling     | Tailwind CSS 4, PostCSS                     |
| UI          | Radix UI primitives, shadcn-style components|
| Forms       | React Hook Form + Zod + @hookform/resolvers |
| Email       | Resend + @react-email/render                |
| Storage     | Supabase Storage                            |
| Analytics   | Vercel Analytics                            |
| Pkg Manager | Bun (always use `bun`, never `npm`)         |

# Build & Dev Commands

```bash
bun run dev        # Start dev server
bun run build      # Production build
bun run start      # Start production server
bun run lint       # ESLint
```

# Architecture

- `proxy.ts` at root handles auth middleware (Next.js 16 replaces middleware.ts)
- `lib/supabase/` has `client.ts` (browser), `server.ts` (server components/actions), `admin.ts` (service role)
- `app/actions/` contains server actions grouped by domain (auth, addresses, admin, stripe, upload)
- `app/api/` contains API routes for webhooks, admin, uploads
- `components/ui/` has ~50 Radix-based primitives — always reuse these, never recreate
- `@/*` path alias maps to project root

# Key Routes

- `/` — Landing page
- `/signin`, `/signup`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password` — Auth flows
- `/dashboard`, `/profile`, `/orders`, `/orders/[id]` — Customer area
- `/schedule`, `/schedule/return`, `/schedule/success` — Pickup scheduling
- `/manage/login`, `/manage/dashboard`, `/manage/orders/[id]` — Admin area

# Supabase Tables

`orders`, `order_items`, `profiles`, `addresses`, `subscriptions`

# Environment Variables

Required: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `ADMIN_USERNAME`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD`

Optional: `SLACK_ORDER_WEBHOOK_URL` (Slack Incoming Webhook — if unset, `server/services/slack.ts` no-ops silently)

# Important Patterns

- Admin auth uses both Supabase `profiles.is_admin` flag AND a session cookie (`admin_session`)
- Stripe webhooks at `/api/webhooks/stripe` handle payment/subscription events
- Image uploads go through Supabase Storage via `lib/supabase/storage.ts` (server-side, using service role key)
- No test framework is configured — do not assume tests exist
